---
import { CONSENT_STORAGE_KEY } from "@trilleo/ui/consent";
import { THEME_STORAGE_KEY } from "@trilleo/ui/theme";
import InfoLayout from "../../layouts/InfoLayout.astro";
import {
  OAUTH_MAX_AGE_S,
  PENDING_MAX_AGE_S,
  WEBAUTHN_MAX_AGE_S,
} from "../../lib/auth/cookies";
import { SESSION_TTL_MS } from "../../lib/auth/sessions";

const sessionDays = SESSION_TTL_MS / (24 * 60 * 60 * 1000);

const sections = [
  { slug: "short", text: "In short" },
  { slug: "cookies", text: "Cookies" },
  { slug: "storage", text: "Browser storage" },
  { slug: "control", text: "Your choices" },
] as const;
---

<InfoLayout path="/legal/cookies/" sections={sections} history>
  <h2 id="short">In short</h2>
  <p>
    The site sets cookies only to sign you in: one while you’re signed in, and
    short-lived ones while you’re signing in. Those are necessary and always on.
    Two things are your choice, from the card you see on your first visit or
    “Cookie settings” at the bottom of every page:
  </p>

  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Preferences</strong> (on unless you turn them off): remembering
      light or dark mode, and keeping tool data and game saves in this browser
      while you’re signed out. Off, they last until you close the tab, and
      turning them off deletes what this browser kept.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Analytics</strong> (off unless you allow it): Cloudflare Web
      Analytics counts page views. It sets no cookies and doesn’t identify you;
      it only loads if you say yes, and never when your browser sends Global
      Privacy Control.
    </li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    None of it tracks you across sites, none of it is shared, and there are no
    advertising cookies.
  </p>

  <h2 id="cookies">Cookies</h2>
  <table>
    <thead>
      <tr>
        <th scope="col">Name</th>
        <th scope="col">What it does</th>
        <th scope="col">How long</th>
      </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr>
        <td>
          <code>__Host-trilleo_session</code>
        </td>
        <td>
          Keeps you signed in. A random token; the server stores only its hash.
          Secure, HTTP-only, same-site.
        </td>
        <td>
          {sessionDays} days, renewed while you use the site; gone when you sign
          out
        </td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>
          <code>trilleo_oauth</code>
        </td>
        <td>
          Protects the trip to GitHub and back while you sign in (a one-time
          check value).
        </td>
        <td>{OAUTH_MAX_AGE_S / 60} minutes, or until you’re back</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>
          <code>__Host-trilleo_sign_in</code>
        </td>
        <td>
          While you sign in by email: the address the code went to, and once
          it’s confirmed for a new account, a one-time value for choosing your
          username.
        </td>
        <td>{PENDING_MAX_AGE_S / 60} minutes, or until you’re signed in</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>
          <code>__Host-trilleo_webauthn</code>
        </td>
        <td>
          While you add or use a passkey: the one-time challenge your device
          signs.
        </td>
        <td>{WEBAUTHN_MAX_AGE_S / 60} minutes, or until it’s used</td>
      </tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
  <p>
    Cloudflare, which delivers the site, may set its own strictly necessary
    security cookie (such as <code>__cf_bm</code>) when it checks for bots.
    Cloudflare’s cookie policy covers it.
  </p>

  <h2 id="storage">Browser storage</h2>
  <p>
    These stay in your browser and are never sent to the server by themselves.
    With preferences off, the ones that remember things go in the tab’s own
    storage (sessionStorage) and vanish when you close it.
  </p>
  <table>
    <thead>
      <tr>
        <th scope="col">Key</th>
        <th scope="col">What it holds</th>
      </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr>
        <td>
          <code>{CONSENT_STORAGE_KEY}</code>
        </td>
        <td>
          Your cookie choices and when you made them (necessary: it’s how the
          site remembers them).
        </td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>
          <code>{THEME_STORAGE_KEY}</code>
        </td>
        <td>
          Light or dark mode, if you chose one with the header toggle. Cleared
          when you switch back to your system’s choice.
        </td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>
          <code>trilleo:tool:…</code>
        </td>
        <td>What you made in a tool (such as notes) while signed out.</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>
          <code>trilleo:game:skygrid</code>
        </td>
        <td>Your Skygrid island while signed out.</td>
      </tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
  <p>
    When you sign in, a tool may offer to move what’s in your browser into your
    account. Nothing moves unless you say so.
  </p>

  <h2 id="control">Your choices</h2>
  <p>
    <a href="/legal/cookies/#control" data-cookie-settings>
      Open cookie settings
    </a>{" "}
    to change what you allowed (it needs JavaScript; without it, nothing
    optional runs). You can also clear cookies and site data in your browser’s
    settings at any time. You’ll be signed out, and anything kept only in your
    browser (tool data and game saves from while you were signed out) will be
    lost, so move it to an account or export it first.
  </p>
</InfoLayout>
